course: dictionary
lesson: 197
title: Al: a name, a symbol and a short form
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Al can be a short name. It is a short form of boys' names like Albert, Alan, Alfred or Alexander. It has a capital A because it is a name, just like Leo or Ella.
explain: In science writing, «et al.» is a Latin phrase that means «and others». It tells you that a book names one author, but there are more people in the group, so Patel «et al.» means Patel and some other scientists.
explain: Small letters in phrases like «al dente» and «et al.» are part of a fixed set of words. A capital A with a symbol like Al is different: in the periodic table it is the chemical symbol for aluminium. Always check the capital letter and the words around it to know which meaning you need.
fact: Al is a short form of boys' names such as Albert, Alan, Alfred and Alexander.
fact: «et al.» is Latin for «and others», and science writers use it when a list of authors is long.
fact: «al dente» is Italian for pasta cooked so it is still a little firm.
fact: Al with a capital A is the chemical symbol for aluminium, a light metal.
fact: «Eid al-Fitr» is the Muslim festival that ends Ramadan, a month of fasting from dawn to sunset.
exercise: Al is a short form of which name? | Alabama | Alexandra | Alder | *Alexander
exercise: In science, what does a capital Al stand for? | *Aluminium | Alarm | Alcohol
exercise: What does «al dente» describe? | *Pasta cooked so it is still a little firm | A song sung in Italy | Pasta that is soggy and overcooked | A boy named Al
test: In a science book, «Patel et al.» is written after one name. What does «et al.» mean? | Patel wrote the book alone | *And others | Patel is a scientist from Italy
test: The festival «Eid al-Fitr» ends which month of fasting? | Diwali | *Ramadan | Christmas
exam: Which element has the chemical symbol Al? | Iron | *Aluminium | Silver | Gold
